# tools/socket/fullcore_ports.golden -- FROZEN port surface of
# M68kFullCoreSynth, captured at the parent commit of the axi-socket
# adapter plan. Design spec section 10 forbids this plan from changing
# it: no port added, none removed, none renamed, none resized.
# Regenerate ONLY with an explicit, reviewed decision:
#   python3 tools/socket/check_socket_netlist.py --regen
#
# RE-BASELINED 2026-09-04 by the walker/D-cache passthrough work -- the ONE
# intended port-surface change of that design, and the only one it makes.
# The 78 itlbAxi_*/dtlbAxi_* ports (39 each) were removed because the ITLB and
# DTLB table walkers no longer emit AXI at all: their three dependent descriptor
# reads and their U/M descriptor writeback are ordinary DcacheService client
# traffic, arbitrated inside LsEuPlugin and issued (when they miss) as the
# D-cache's own refill / write-through. That is 78 of the previous 205 ports --
# 38% of the synthesised port surface -- and it retires two AXI masters, the
# AR=2/AW=3 walker ID collision, and two AxiDMerge owner tiers along with them.
# 199 -> 121 ports. (The 2026-09-03 revalidation predicted "205 -> 127"; that
# arithmetic counted this file's own 6 comment lines as ports. The real port
# count before this change was 199.)
